cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both this repository (this file)
  and the manuscript listed under preferred-citation.
type: software
title: >-
  Pacific-Antarctic Ridge Meander Analysis: code and supporting figures
  for "Standing Meanders of the Antarctic Circumpolar Current: Evidence
  for Ridge-Controlled Eddy Saturation"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-05-28"
license: MIT
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/xinlongliu0307/southern-ocean-pacific-antarctic-ridge-meander-trends
abstract: >-
  Datasets, MATLAB functions, and figures used in the analysis of standing
  meanders of the Antarctic Circumpolar Current over the Pacific-Antarctic
  Ridge. The analyses combine satellite altimetry, the Roemmich-Gilson Argo
  climatology, and CMEMS surface geostrophic velocities to document meander
  position, width, intensity, and associated eddy kinetic energy over
  1993-2023. The repository includes data folders with monthly meander
  positions and north/south boundary latitudes, and eight numbered MATLAB
  scripts implementing the Argo 4D-cube construction, the gyre ADT trend,
  the Mann-Kendall and modified Mann-Kendall tests, the EKE trend
  analysis, the meander width-speed decomposition, the Theil-Sen
  estimator, and the publication-figure plotting routines.

